CLASS aeb net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/storage/RegionFile
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  Region File Format
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  Concept: The minimum unit of storage on hard drives is 4KB. 90% of Minecraft
	COMMENT  chunks are smaller than 4KB. 99% are smaller than 8KB. Write a simple
	COMMENT  container to store chunks in single files in runs of 4KB sectors.
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  Each region file represents a 32x32 group of chunks. The conversion from
	COMMENT  chunk number to region number is floor(coord / 32): a chunk at (30, -3)
	COMMENT  would be in region (0, -1), and one at (70, -30) would be at (3, -1).
	COMMENT  Region files are named "r.x.z.data", where x and z are the region coordinates.
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  A region file begins with a 4KB header that describes where chunks are stored
	COMMENT  in the file. A 4-byte big-endian integer represents sector offsets and sector
	COMMENT  counts. The chunk offset for a chunk (x, z) begins at byte 4*(x+z*32) in the
	COMMENT  file. The bottom byte of the chunk offset indicates the number of sectors the
	COMMENT  chunk takes up, and the top 3 bytes represent the sector number of the chunk.
	COMMENT  Given a chunk offset o, the chunk data begins at byte 4096*(o/256) and takes up
	COMMENT  at most 4096*(o%256) bytes. A chunk cannot exceed 1MB in size. If a chunk
	COMMENT  offset is 0, the corresponding chunk is not stored in the region file.
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  Chunk data begins with a 4-byte big-endian integer representing the chunk data
	COMMENT  length in bytes, not counting the length field. The length must be smaller than
	COMMENT  4096 times the number of sectors. The next byte is a version field, to allow
	COMMENT  backwards-compatible updates to how chunks are encoded.
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  A version of 1 represents a gzipped NBT file. The gzipped data is the chunk
	COMMENT  length - 1.
	COMMENT
	COMMENT  A version of 2 represents a deflated (zlib compressed) NBT file. The deflated
	COMMENT  data is the chunk length - 1.
	FIELD a emptySector [B
	FIELD b fileName Ljava/io/File;
	FIELD c file Ljava/io/RandomAccessFile;
	FIELD d offsets [I
	FIELD e chunkTimestamps [I
	FIELD f sectorFree Ljava/util/ArrayList;
	FIELD g sizeDelta I
	FIELD h lastModified J
	METHOD <init> (Ljava/io/File;)V
		ARG 1 path
	METHOD a getChunkDataInputStream (II)Ljava/io/DataInputStream;
		COMMENT gets an (uncompressed) stream representing the chunk data returns null if
		COMMENT the chunk is not found or an error occurs
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
	METHOD a setOffset (III)V
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
		ARG 3 offset
	METHOD a write (II[BI)V
		COMMENT write a chunk at (x,z) with length bytes of data to disk
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
		ARG 3 data
		ARG 4 length
	METHOD a write (I[BI)V
		COMMENT write a chunk data to the region file at specified sector number
		ARG 1 sectorNumber
		ARG 2 data
		ARG 3 length
	METHOD b getChunkDataOutputStream (II)Ljava/io/DataOutputStream;
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
	METHOD b setTimestamp (III)V
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
		ARG 3 value
	METHOD c close ()V
	METHOD c hasChunk (II)Z
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
	METHOD d outOfBounds (II)Z
		COMMENT is this an invalid chunk coordinate?
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
	METHOD e getOffset (II)I
		ARG 1 x
		ARG 2 z
